      "message": "DRY-ing the FFI (some calls were duplicated between `FdtNode` and `FdtNodeMut` or between different methods), removing the need to play tricks around the borrow checker because we\u0027re constrained by the high-level API (e.g. `getprop_internal()`), addressing numerous unsafe behaviors, and allowing said high-level API to be reworked without having to deal with hundreds of LoCs interleaved with (duplicated) FFI is, on its own, a good justification for this series, IMO.\n\nI\u0027m planning to rework the API for mutable accesses to the `Fdt` because `FdtNodeMut` in its current format is too constraining and forces us to write counter-intuitive, suboptimal, and confusing code (e.g. in aosp/2944351 or aosp/2879975).\n\n`FdtOwned` is an example of something else that could implement the traits but I agree that we might not implement it that way. That wouldn\u0027t undermine the value of the above.",
